    "result_text": "All 278 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, including the `Cp17Tests` acceptance test for this feature.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` pipeline now computes a `sharesHousehold` flag. Since the acceptance test reads the value back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` (not just the create response), the flag must be **persisted**, matching the existing `namesakeCount` pattern rather than being response-only.\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `Boolean sharesHousehold` field (`@Column(name = \"shares_household\")`) with getter/setter.\n2. **Schema SQL** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `shares_household` column (`BOOLEAN` / `BIT(1)` for mysql). Tests run on hsqldb.\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `sharesHousehold` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct maps it automatically by name.\n4. **`AssignOwnerSharesHousehold.java`** (new) \u2014 an OfficeFloor step that sets the flag to `true` when another existing owner (excluding self) already has the same address **and** city, else `false`. Modeled on `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`.\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignSharesHousehold` step (under `transaction` governance) between `assignNamesakeCount` and `save`, so it runs before persistence and the owner is always created.\n\nThe change is purely additive and never rejects creation, satisfying \"Still allow the creation.\"",
